{"id": "live-064", "title": "C.D. Smith Construction, Inc. v. The Edison SPE LLC (Milwaukee Mass-Timber Tower Construction-Lien Foreclosure)", "category": "lending-foreclosure", "status": "ruling", "date": "2026-06-29", "jurisdiction": "Milwaukee County Circuit Court", "state": "WI", "amount": "$11.3M default judgment on a $13.67M unpaid construction claim", "source": "live", "source_url": "https://www.enr.com/articles/63313-contractor-wins-113m-judgment-in-milwaukee-timber-tower-lawsuit", "summary": "Milwaukee County Circuit Court Judge Glenn H. Yamahiro entered a default judgment of more than $11.3 million on June 29, 2026 in favor of general contractor C.D. Smith Construction against The Edison SPE LLC, a Neutral affiliate, clearing the way to foreclose on a construction lien against the stalled 31-story Edison mass-timber tower site in downtown Milwaukee. The default arose after Neutral CEO Nate Helbach filed a pro se mediation/arbitration request the court struck because a corporation cannot represent itself in litigation.", "significance": "The ruling gives C.D. Smith a direct path to force a sale of the Edison site via lien foreclosure rather than standing as an unsecured creditor, and is a reminder that developers must respond to litigation through licensed counsel or risk default judgment on the full amount claimed regardless of the underlying merits.", "judge": "Glenn H. Yamahiro", "tags": ["construction lien", "foreclosure", "mass timber", "default judgment", "wisconsin"]}
